)PANEL KEYLIST(ISRHELP,ISR)
)ATTR DEFAULT(%+_)
/*********************************************************************/
/* PANEL    : MBKAMLH                                                */
/* TITLE    : HELP - AML RULE PARAMETERS                             */
/*-------------------------------------------------------------------*/
/* 2009-09-14 AOS  ORIGINAL                                          */
/*********************************************************************/
  % TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE) SKIP(ON)
  + TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN) SKIP(ON)
  ] TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) SKIP(ON)
)BODY EXPAND(//) WIDTH(80)
%TUTORIAL -/-/- AML RULE PARAMETERS -/-/- TUTORIAL
%Command ===>_ZCMD                                                             +
+
+RGAML010 checks yesterday's hard postings against seven rules and raises
+alerts for the MLRO team.  The defaults are in the program; this dialog
+maintains overrides in MBK.PRD.CNTL(AMLRULES).
+
]Rules+
+  %R01+large cash: one cash credit >= threshold
+  %R02+structuring: >= count cash credits each below R01, total >= threshold
+  %R03+rapid movement: credits >= threshold and 90% out the same day
+  %R04+high risk customer: any transaction >= threshold
+  %R05+dormant reactivation: debits >= threshold within 30 days
+  %R06+international: SWIFT out total >= threshold
+  %R07+velocity: >= count Faster Payments out (threshold not used)
+
]Who may change them+
+   Anyone with AML authority may view.  Only the MLRO and nominated
+   deputy (level M) may SAVE, quoting the decision reference.  Switching
+   a rule off or raising a threshold above 150% of default needs a second
+   confirmation and is reported to the Financial Crime Committee.
+
]RERUN+  resubmits RGAML01 (operations override needed) after a change
+   that must apply to today's postings.  Alerts are one per account per
+   rule per day, so a rerun does not duplicate alerts.
)PROC
  &ZUP = MBKMENUH
)END
